```java
@Service
class RegistrationService {
    private final UserRepository users;
    private final PasswordEncoder passwordEncoder;

    void register(String email, char[] rawPassword) {
        String verifier = passwordEncoder.encode(CharBuffer.wrap(rawPassword));
        users.save(new User(email, verifier));
        Arrays.fill(rawPassword, '\0');
    }

    boolean passwordMatches(User user, CharSequence candidate) {
        return passwordEncoder.matches(candidate, user.passwordHash());
    }
}
```
*Store only the encoded verifier. Never log either the password or its candidate value, and do not compare a newly encoded value with `equals` because modern encoders generate a fresh salt.*

